					<Id>1794003493425</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[varDisplayRandom]]></Name>
					<Description><![CDATA[A random number generator independent of AnyLogic's. It has to be on Main so that it doesn't reset its sequence every time it is called. AnyLogic's own generators persist in the background so they don't have this problem. We need this generator to be separate from AnyLogic's so that it doesn't influence the simulation results by ticking the AnlyLogic random generator sequence; this jitter can be turned off and the simulation results won't change.]]></Description>
					<X>390</X><Y>890</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
