				</Variable>
				<Variable Class="PlainVariable">
					<Id>1794102463334</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[varDensityKernel]]></Name>
					<Description><![CDATA[An array for each grid position that stores Sum(e^(-d/r)) for that position, where the sum is of e^(-d/r) for all neighbouring positions within a cutoff range.

d=distance from current gridpoint (metres)
r=parRentInfluenceDecayLength

cutoff=parRentInfluenceDecayLength * parRentInfluenceDecayLength_CutoffMultiple

This kernel is used for each position when adding up land area and population count on all neighbouring grid points within the range to calculate density - rather than just using density on a single node - to smooth over density relationships between nodes because values in the kernel are distance based exponential decays).

]]></Description>
					<X>120</X><Y>2330</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Properties SaveInSnapshot="true" Constant="false" AccessType="public" StaticVariable="false">
