						<Name><![CDATA[msg]]></Name>
						<Type><![CDATA[String]]></Type>
					</Parameter>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). Arguments: msg (String)
// Prints msg to the Console only when parShowTestOutput (Main parameter, boolean) is true.
// Used for test output in functions that run every turn, so all of it can be switched off with one toggle.
// Warnings that must always show still use traceln directly.
if (parShowTestOutput) traceln(msg);
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>RETURNS_VALUE</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[boolean]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1793953190574</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funInvest]]></Name>
					<X>800</X><Y>1320</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Returns value, type: boolean. No arguments. Called by funRunCheckpoint at each spread equilibrium
// when welfare hasn't peaked yet (funCheckWelfarePeak), straight after funAssignTraffic, so flows are fresh.
// Upgrades parNumUpgrades links. Link costs are not considered.
// Returns true if any link's impedance changed, false if no link could be upgraded at all (funRunCheckpoint then ends the run).
//
// Each upgrade:
//   1. Draw a link at random, weighted by score V/C: congested links are favoured, regardless of how much traffic they carry
//      (so busy central links don't win just for their volume).
//      Links with no flow score 0 and are never drawn. Each link can be drawn at most once per investment
//      (scores aren't recomputed between draws, since flows only change at the next assignment).
//   2. New impedance = current - parUpgradeAggresiveness, but never below parImpedanceMin.
//   3. Land check: the wider road must not push either end node's land below parMinAvailableLand.
//      If it would, the link is instead upgraded as far as the land allows (if at all), then blacklisted.
//      That partial upgrade doesn't count towards parNumUpgrades, so an investment can upgrade slightly more than planned.
//   4. Otherwise apply the full step with funApplyImpedanceChange (capacity, travel time, end-node land, nearby density and rent).
//      A link that reaches parImpedanceMin is blacklisted too.
// Blacklisted links (Link variable varUpgradeBlocked) are never drawn again. Blacklisting is permanent: impedance only
// goes down and roads only take more land. Stops early if no link is left to draw.
//
// Land-limited impedance: road land at each end node is A * lanes, with A = 0.5 * parRoadWidthRef * L * parCarLandUsage
// (land per lane) and lanes = parImpedanceLocal / I. With slack S = the smaller of the two end nodes'
// (parCellLand - road land - parMinAvailableLand), the road may grow by at most S:  A * (lanes_new - lanes) <= S
//   =>  lanes_new = lanes + S / A,   I_new = parImpedanceLocal / lanes_new
//
// Random draws use the investment's own generator varInvestRandom, so investing doesn't shift the random sequence of
// the relocations (which would mix the investment's effect with random-number noise when comparing runs).
// Uses:
//   Main parameters  parNumUpgrades (int), parUpgradeAggresiveness (double, impedance subtracted per upgrade), parImpedanceMin
//   Main variable    varInvestRandom (java.util.Random, initial value: new java.util.Random(parSeed + 3))
//   Link variable    varUpgradeBlocked (boolean, initial value false)

Set<Link> drawn = new HashSet<>();   // links already drawn in this investment (upgraded or blacklisted)
int upgrades = 0;          // full steps (count towards parNumUpgrades)
int partialUpgrades = 0;   // land-limited upgrades just before blacklisting (don't count)
int blacklisted = 0;
while (upgrades < parNumUpgrades) {
    // 1. Weighted draw among links not blacklisted, not yet drawn, and carrying flow
    double total = 0;
    for (Link l : links) {
        if (l.varUpgradeBlocked || drawn.contains(l) || l.varFlowVol <= 0) continue;
        total += l.varFlowVol / l.varCapacity;
    }
    if (total <= 0) break;   // nothing left to upgrade
    double r = varInvestRandom.nextDouble() * total;   // random point along the stacked scores
    Link pick = null;
    for (Link l : links) {
        if (l.varUpgradeBlocked || drawn.contains(l) || l.varFlowVol <= 0) continue;
        pick = l;   // keeps the last eligible link in case rounding leaves r just past the end
        r -= l.varFlowVol / l.varCapacity;
        if (r < 0) break;
    }
    drawn.add(pick);

    // 2. New impedance
    if (pick.varImpedance <= parImpedanceMin) {   // already at the minimum: can't be upgraded
        pick.varUpgradeBlocked = true;
        blacklisted++;
        continue;
    }
    double newImpedance = max(parImpedanceMin, pick.varImpedance - parUpgradeAggresiveness);

    // 3. Land check at both end nodes (unfloored land, same formula as GridPoint.funUpdateAvailableLand)
    double landPerLane = 0.5 * parRoadWidthRef * pick.parLength * parCarLandUsage;   // road land per lane pair, at each end node
    double slack = Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY;                                          // land each end node can still give up (smaller of the two)
    for (GridPoint g : new GridPoint[] {pick.parNodeA, pick.parNodeB}) {
        double roadLand = 0;
        for (Link l : g.colLinks) roadLand += l.funNodeRoadLand();
        slack = min(slack, parCellLand - roadLand - parMinAvailableLand);
    }
    double updatedLanes = parImpedanceLocal / newImpedance;
    double extraRoadLand = landPerLane * (updatedLanes - pick.varLanes);
    if (extraRoadLand > slack) {   // full step needs too much land: upgrade as far as the land allows, then blacklist
        if (slack > 0) {
            double landLimitedImpedance = parImpedanceLocal / (pick.varLanes + slack / landPerLane);
            funApplyImpedanceChange(pick, landLimitedImpedance);
            partialUpgrades++;
        }
        pick.varUpgradeBlocked = true; // If there was some land left, if statement above fills it with road, then we block it from future upgrades here. If there already was no land left, then jump straight to blocking it here.
        blacklisted++;
        continue;
    }

    // 4. Apply the full step
    funApplyImpedanceChange(pick, newImpedance);
    upgrades++;
    if (newImpedance <= parImpedanceMin) {   // reached the minimum: no further upgrades possible
        pick.varUpgradeBlocked = true;
        blacklisted++;
    }
}

funRuntimePrint("Investment at turn " + varTurnCount + " (round " + varRounds + "): "
				+ upgrades + " of " + parNumUpgrades + " links upgraded, " + partialUpgrades + " land-limited upgrades, "
      			+ blacklisted + " newly blacklisted" + (upgrades < parNumUpgrades ? " (no more upgradable links)" : ""));
return upgrades + partialUpgrades > 0;
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[Agent]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794003568002</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funPlaceIcon]]></Name>
					<X>390</X><Y>910</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Parameter>
						<Name><![CDATA[ag]]></Name>
						<Type><![CDATA[Agent]]></Type>
					</Parameter>
					<Parameter>
						<Name><![CDATA[g]]></Name>
						<Type><![CDATA[GridPoint]]></Type>
					</Parameter>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). Arguments: ag (Agent), g (GridPoint)
// Display only: puts agent ag's icon at a random spot near node g instead of exactly on it, so agents sharing a node stay visible.
// The spot is uniform within a circle of radius parIconJitter * parSpacing around the node (parIconJitter = 0 puts it back on the node).
// Uses its own random generator (Main variable varDisplayRandom, type java.util.Random), not the model's,
// so icon positions never change the simulation's random draws: results are identical with or without jitter.
double radius = parIconJitter * parSpacing * sqrt(varDisplayRandom.nextDouble());   // sqrt spreads points evenly over the circle's area, instead of bunching them at the centre
double angle = 2 * PI * varDisplayRandom.nextDouble();
ag.setXY(g.getX() + radius * cos(angle), g.getY() + radius * sin(angle));
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794008472587</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[testPrintSpread]]></Name>
					<X>720</X><Y>1380</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// TEMPORARY TEST. Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). No arguments. Called by funPrintFinalReports.
// Prints the citizens' final spread (funComputeSpread: standard distance of their homes from their centroid, metres)
// and its % change from the first equilibrium (varFirstEquilibriumSpread, recorded once by funResumeFromEquilibrium).
// Final spread = mean of the last parSpreadEquilibriumWindow values in colAverageSpread (the reports since the last
// investment), which smooths out turn-to-turn noise; if that history is empty, the current spread is used instead.
// The % change is stored in varSpreadChangePercent (Main variable, double, initial value 0), for experiments to read after the run.
// It stays 0 if no equilibrium was reached (no baseline).
double current = funComputeSpread();
double finalSpread = current;
String source = "most recent reading";
int n = colAverageSpread.size();
if (n > 0) {
    int window = min(parSpreadEquilibriumWindow, n);
    double sum = 0;
    for (int i = n - window; i < n; i++) sum += colAverageSpread.get(i);
    finalSpread = sum / window;
    source = "mean reading of last " + window + " reports";
}
String s = "Turn " + varTurnCount + " citizens' spread from their centroid: " + roundToDecimal(finalSpread, 0) + " m (source: " + source + ")";
if (varFirstEquilibriumSpread > 0) {
    varSpreadChangePercent = 100 * (finalSpread - varFirstEquilibriumSpread) / varFirstEquilibriumSpread;   // Main variable (double): kept for experiments to read after the run
    s += ", first equilibrium " + roundToDecimal(varFirstEquilibriumSpread, 0) + " m, change " + (varSpreadChangePercent >= 0 ? "+" : "") + roundToDecimal(varSpreadChangePercent, 1) + "%";
}
else s += " (no equilibrium reached, so no baseline to compare with)";
funRuntimePrint(s);   // TEST
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794009166903</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funRuntimePrint]]></Name>
					<X>800</X><Y>1060</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Parameter>
						<Name><![CDATA[msg]]></Name>
						<Type><![CDATA[String]]></Type>
					</Parameter>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). Arguments: msg (String)
// Prints msg to the Console only when parShowRuntimeOutput (Main parameter, boolean) is true.
// Used for runtime monitoring output (e.g. density after each assignment), so it can be switched on and off
// separately from the test output controlled by parShowTestOutput (funTestPrint).
// Warnings that must always show still use traceln directly.
if (parShowRuntimeOutput) traceln(msg);]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794029988652</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[testPrintUtilityShares]]></Name>
					<X>580</X><Y>1380</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// TEMPORARY TEST. Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). No arguments. Called by the cyclic test report event in Main.
// Shows whether any utility term dominates or is negligible, using the sub-utilities each agent stored on its last turn.
// For each agent: share of term i = |U_i| / sum_j |U_j|  (absolute values, since privacy can be positive when VOP < 0).
// Prints the average share of each term over agents, the average size of each term in rand per month,
// and the average expected welfare (logsum, varExpectedWelfare) over the same agents.
// Agents that haven't had a turn yet (all stored sub-utilities still 0) are left out.

// Citizens: rent, travel cost, travel time, privacy
double[] cShare = new double[4];
double[] cSize = new double[4];
double cWelfare = 0;
int nC = 0;
for (Citizen c : citizens) {
    double[] u = {c.varURent, c.varUTravelCost, c.varUTravelTime, c.varUPriv};
    double sumAbs = 0;
    for (double x : u) sumAbs += abs(x);
    if (sumAbs == 0) continue;   // no turn yet
    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
        cShare[i] += abs(u[i]) / sumAbs;
        cSize[i] += u[i];
    }
    cWelfare += c.varExpectedWelfare;
    nC++;
}
if (nC > 0) {
    String[] names = {"rent", "travel cost", "travel time", "privacy"};
    String s = "Turn " + varTurnCount + " citizen utility shares (" + nC + " citizens):";
    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) s += " " + names[i] + " " + roundToDecimal(100 * cShare[i] / nC, 1) + "% (avg " + roundToDecimal(cSize[i] / nC, 0) + ")";
    s += "; avg expected welfare " + roundToDecimal(cWelfare / nC, 0);
    funRuntimePrint(s);   // TEST
}

// Activities: rent, location
double[] aShare = new double[2];
double[] aSize = new double[2];
double aWelfare = 0;
int nA = 0;
for (Activity a : activities) {
    double[] u = {a.varURent, a.varULoc};
    double sumAbs = abs(u[0]) + abs(u[1]);
    if (sumAbs == 0) continue;   // no turn yet
    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
        aShare[i] += abs(u[i]) / sumAbs;
        aSize[i] += u[i];
    }
    aWelfare += a.varExpectedWelfare;
    nA++;
}
if (nA > 0) {
    funRuntimePrint("Turn " + varTurnCount + " activity utility shares (" + nA + " activities): rent " + roundToDecimal(100 * aShare[0] / nA, 1)
            + "% (avg " + roundToDecimal(aSize[0] / nA, 0) + "), location " + roundToDecimal(100 * aShare[1] / nA, 1) + "% (avg " + roundToDecimal(aSize[1] / nA, 0) + "); avg expected welfare " + roundToDecimal(aWelfare / nA, 0));   // TEST
}
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>RETURNS_VALUE</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[boolean]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794035417322</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funCheckSpreadEquilibrium]]></Name>
					<X>580</X><Y>1330</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Returns value, type: boolean. No arguments. Called by funRunCheckpoint.
// Equilibrium check on the citizens' spread: the standard distance of their homes from the citizens' mean position (centroid),
// calculated by funComputeSpread (metres; the 2D standard deviation of positions).
// Every report's spread is appended to colAverageSpread (Collection in Main: ArrayList of Double), a growing history.
// The mean of the last N = parSpreadEquilibriumWindow reports (this one included) is compared with the mean of the N reports before them:
//   relative change = |recent mean - previous mean| / previous mean
// Averaging both sides smooths out report-to-report noise, while comparing two consecutive windows still catches
// a slow steady trend (the recent window's mean sits above or below the previous one's until the spread plateaus).
// If the change is within parSpreadEquilibriumTolerance (e.g. 0.05 = 5%), prints the spread and returns true; otherwise returns false.
// What happens at equilibrium (invest or end the run) is decided by the caller, funRunCheckpoint.
// Until there are 2N reports in the history, it only stores the spread.
// The caller clears colAverageSpread after an investment, so the next equilibrium is judged only on post-investment reports.

double current = funComputeSpread();   // spread in metres

colAverageSpread.add(current);             // stored for this and later reports' comparisons
int window = parSpreadEquilibriumWindow;
int n = colAverageSpread.size();
if (n < 2 * window) return false;          // not enough history yet for two full windows

double sumRecent = 0, sumPrevious = 0;
for (int i = n - window; i < n; i++) sumRecent += colAverageSpread.get(i);                    // last 'window' reports, this one included
for (int i = n - 2 * window; i < n - window; i++) sumPrevious += colAverageSpread.get(i);     // the 'window' reports before those
double recentMean = sumRecent / window;
double previousMean = sumPrevious / window;
double change = abs(recentMean - previousMean) / previousMean;
if (change > parSpreadEquilibriumTolerance) return false;   // still changing: keep running

String s = "Spread equilibrium reached at turn " + varTurnCount + " (round " + varRounds + "): citizens' spread from their centroid "
        + roundToDecimal(recentMean, 0) + " m (mean of last " + window + " reports), change vs the " + window + " reports before: " + roundToDecimal(100 * change, 5) + "% (tolerance "
        + roundToDecimal(100 * parSpreadEquilibriumTolerance, 5) + "%)";
// % change vs the first equilibrium (varFirstEquilibriumSpread, set by funResumeFromEquilibrium; still 0 at the first equilibrium itself)
if (varFirstEquilibriumSpread > 0) {
    double changeFromFirst = 100 * (recentMean - varFirstEquilibriumSpread) / varFirstEquilibriumSpread;
    s += ", change vs first equilibrium (" + roundToDecimal(varFirstEquilibriumSpread, 0) + " m): " + (changeFromFirst >= 0 ? "+" : "") + roundToDecimal(changeFromFirst, 1) + "%";
}
funRuntimePrint(s);
return true;
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794039394156</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funPrintFinalReports]]></Name>
					<X>580</X><Y>1400</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Parameter>
						<Name><![CDATA[reason]]></Name>
						<Type><![CDATA[String]]></Type>
					</Parameter>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). Arguments: reason (String)
// Prints why the run is ending, then the end-of-run reports. Does not stop the simulation: the caller calls finishSimulation() afterwards.
// Called from every stop point (equilibrium with no investment made in funRunCheckpoint, parMaxRounds reached in funSimulateNextTurn),
// so every run ends with the same reports whichever condition stops it. Add or remove end-of-run reports here.
// Also called from Main's On destroy (Stop button), guarded by varReportPrinted so the reports never print twice:
//   if (!varReportPrinted) funPrintFinalReports("stopped manually");
funRuntimePrint("Run ended at turn " + varTurnCount + " (round " + varRounds + "): " + reason);
testPrintUtilityShares();
testPrintVCRatio();
testPrintSpread();
varReportPrinted = true;   // Main boolean: stops On destroy printing the reports again
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794044476645</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funRunCheckpoint]]></Name>
					<Description><![CDATA[Checks for density equilibrium (with another function), decides to invest or end the simulation, and calls for final reports to be printed.]]></Description>
					<X>720</X><Y>1160</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>true</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). No arguments. Called by funSimulateNextTurn at appropriate intervals, and on start up when loading a saved state.
// At each checkpoint: 
//   - Terminate simulation if maximum rounds parMaxRounds have happened. Otherwise:
//   - Check if spread has reached equilibrium, return if it hasn't. Otherwise:
//   - The first equilibrium is saved to savedState.txt (funSaveState), if this state hasn't been saved or loaded already
//     (varStateSaved). The network is always on file (loaded from, or just saved to, savedNetwork.txt). It is then followed by
//     funResumeFromEquilibrium, the same restart a run loading this state goes through, so both continue identically.
//   - Traffic is assigned, and then we check if welfare has passed its peak, and either finish simulation if it has, or run an investment if it has not.
//     If funInvest finds no link it can upgrade, the run ends (no welfare peak reached).
if (varInitialising) return;   // initialisation phase (funSimulateNextTurn): no spread history, investment or stopping yet.
boolean settled;
if (varAtLoadedEquilibrium) { // For runs loading from saved state file
    settled = true;
    varAtLoadedEquilibrium = false;   // only the first checkpoint after loading will run this if block
    funRuntimePrint("Starting from the loaded equilibrium at turn " + varTurnCount);
}
else settled = funCheckSpreadEquilibrium();

if (varTurnCount >= parMaxRounds * (parNumCitizens + parNumActivities)) {
    funPrintFinalReports("max rounds reached");
    varShowGraphics = true;
    finishSimulation();
    return;
}
if (!settled) return;   // still settling

if (!varStateSaved) {
    funSaveState();
    varStateSaved = true;
    funResumeFromEquilibrium();   // same restart as a run that loads this state, so both continue identically from here
}

// both loaded and through-run paths: fresh flows + access times for the settled city. 
//Future checkpoints coming from either also need this, because they will either be ending the simulation and need final data, or will be performing an investment.
funAssignTraffic();                       
varAssignmentCount++;
varRelocationsSinceAssignment = 0;
if (funCheckWelfarePeak()) {
    funPrintFinalReports("Welfare peaked, no further investment");
    varShowGraphics = true;   // show the final graphics only
    finishSimulation();
}
//If no welfare peak, then invest, and wait for next spread equilibrium to check welfare peak or invest again.
else if (!funInvest()) {   // no link could be upgraded: nothing more to do
    funPrintFinalReports("No upgradable links left before a welfare peak was reached");
    varShowGraphics = true;
    finishSimulation();
}
else {
    funAssignTraffic(); // Assign according to upgraded network.
    varAssignmentCount++;
    varRelocationsSinceAssignment = 0;
    colAverageSpread.clear();
}
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794182497789</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funStartRunLog]]></Name>
					<X>720</X><Y>1480</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). No arguments. Call as the FIRST line of Main's On startup.
// Copies everything printed to the Console (traceln, funTestPrint, funRuntimePrint) into a new text file for this run,
// runs/run_<date>_<time>.txt inside the model folder, while still printing to the Console as normal.
// Writes all of Main's parameter values at the top of the file first.
// Needs two Main variables (type Other): varConsoleOut (java.io.PrintStream) and varLogFile (java.io.PrintStream).
// funStopRunLog (in Main's On destroy) puts the Console back and closes the file.
try {
    java.io.File dir = new java.io.File("runs");
    dir.mkdirs();   // create the runs folder if it doesn't exist yet
    String stamp = new java.text.SimpleDateFormat("yyyy-MM-dd_HHmmss").format(new java.util.Date());
    java.io.File f = new java.io.File(dir, "run_" + stamp + ".txt");
    varLogFile = new java.io.PrintStream(new java.io.FileOutputStream(f), true);
    varConsoleOut = System.out;   // the Console's own stream, kept so it can be restored at the end

    // Parameters first, so the file records the settings that produced the output below
    varLogFile.println("Run log " + stamp);
    varLogFile.println("Parameters:");
    for (String name : getParameterNames()) varLogFile.println("  " + name + " = " + getParameter(name));
    varLogFile.println();

    // From now on, every printed line goes to both the Console and the file
    java.io.PrintStream console = varConsoleOut;
    java.io.PrintStream file = varLogFile;
    System.setOut(new java.io.PrintStream(new java.io.OutputStream() {
        public void write(int b) { console.write(b); file.write(b); }
        public void write(byte[] b, int off, int len) { console.write(b, off, len); file.write(b, off, len); }
        public void flush() { console.flush(); file.flush(); }
    }, true));
    traceln("Logging this run to " + f.getAbsolutePath());
} catch (Exception e) {
    traceln("Could not start run log: " + e.getMessage());
}
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794182514661</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funStopRunLog]]></Name>
					<X>720</X><Y>1500</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). No arguments. Call as the LAST line of Main's On destroy.
// Puts the Console's own output stream back (so the next run doesn't stack a second copy onto this one) and closes this run's log file.
if (varConsoleOut != null) System.setOut(varConsoleOut);
if (varLogFile != null) varLogFile.close();
varConsoleOut = null;
varLogFile = null;
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794209243378</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funSaveState]]></Name>
					<X>-160</X><Y>1260</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). No arguments. Called by funRunCheckpoint at the first spread equilibrium.
// Saves the settled city to savedState.txt in the model folder (overwritten each time), so later runs can start from it
// with funLoadState instead of waiting for the first equilibrium again. The state belongs to the network in savedNetwork.txt,
// which is always this run's network: either loaded from it, or built and saved to it by funBuildNetwork.
// Saved: every Main parameter (to check the state still matches the settings when loading), then
//   CITIZEN  home node index, VOT, VOM, VOP, expected welfare (logsum from its last turn, used by funCheckWelfarePeak),
//            then one weight per activity
//   ACTIVITY location node index, VOM, VOL          (in population order, so weight positions still match activities)
//   LINK     node A index, node B index, impedance, flow
// Land, density, rent and travel times are not saved: they are rebuilt from these after loading.
// Numbers are written with Java's own formatting (always '.' as decimal point), so they read back exactly.
// Switched off by parSaveState (Main parameter, boolean): set it false in experiments, so runs don't overwrite each other's
// saved state (or clash writing the same file when running in parallel). The run itself continues identically either way.
if (!parSaveState) {
    funRuntimePrint("State not saved (parSaveState is false)");
    return;
}
try (java.io.PrintWriter out = new java.io.PrintWriter("savedState.txt")) {
    out.println("SAVED_STATE turn " + varTurnCount + " round " + varRounds);
    for (String name : getParameterNames()) out.println("PARAM\t" + name + "\t" + getParameter(name));
    for (Citizen c : citizens) {
        StringBuilder s = new StringBuilder("CITIZEN\t" + c.varHome.parIndex + "\t" + c.parVOT + "\t" + c.parVOM + "\t" + c.parVOP + "\t" + c.varExpectedWelfare);
        for (double w : c.varActivityWeights) s.append("\t").append(w);
        out.println(s);
    }
    for (Activity a : activities) out.println("ACTIVITY\t" + a.varLocation.parIndex + "\t" + a.parVOM + "\t" + a.parVOL);
    for (Link l : links) out.println("LINK\t" + l.parNodeA.parIndex + "\t" + l.parNodeB.parIndex + "\t" + l.varImpedance + "\t" + l.varFlowVol);
    funRuntimePrint("State saved to savedState.txt at turn " + varTurnCount + " (round " + varRounds + ")");
} catch (Exception e) {
    traceln("Could not save state: " + e.getMessage());
}
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>RETURNS_VALUE</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[boolean]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794209259781</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funLoadState]]></Name>
					<X>-160</X><Y>1280</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Returns value, type: boolean. No arguments. Called by Main on startup, in place of funInitImpedance and
// funPlaceAgents, only when the road network was loaded from savedNetwork.txt and parLoadSavedState is true.
// Recreates the city saved by funSaveState (savedState.txt) at its first spread equilibrium: citizens and activities
// with their saved locations and preferences, and every link's impedance and flow.
// Returns true if loaded; false if there is no usable file, in which case nothing has been created and the
// caller places agents as normal (funPlaceAgents).
//
// The file is only used if it matches this run:
//   - Every Main parameter must have the same value as when it was saved, except those in 'ignored' below
//     (investment, display, output and run-control settings, which don't affect how the city settled). Edit that list as needed.
//   - Every saved link must exist in the current network, and the link counts must match (same savedNetwork.txt).
// After loading:
//   - Preferences are not drawn for loaded agents (funPlaceAgents does that, not the agents' On startup): the saved values are set directly.
//   - Each citizen's expected welfare is restored too, so the first welfare-peak check sees the same values as the straight-through run.
//   - The initialisation phase is skipped (varInitialising = false), the state is not saved again (varStateSaved = true),
//     and the first checkpoint goes straight to investment (varAtLoadedEquilibrium = true), since the city is already settled.
// Main on startup then sets up land and calls funResumeFromEquilibrium (reseed with parSeed + 2, density, queue,
// counters), the same restart the straight-through run goes through at its first equilibrium, so both continue identically.

java.io.File f = new java.io.File("savedState.txt");
if (!f.exists()) {
    traceln("No saved state found: placing agents as normal");
    return false;
}

String[] ignored = {"parRoadUpgradeCost", "parInvestmentRate", "parShowTestOutput", "parShowRuntimeOutput", "parIconJitter",
                    "parMaxRdPx", "parMinRdPx", "parRentColourScaleMultiple", "parMaxRounds", "parMinRounds",
                    "parLoadSavedNetwork", "parLoadSavedState", "parSaveState", "parRelocationInterval", "parParallelAssignment", "parWelfareSlopeWindow", "parWelfareSlopeThreshold",
                    "parNumUpgrades", "parUpgradeAggresiveness",
                    "parRentRef", "parRentMin", "parDensityRef", "parCarLandUsage", "parRentInfluenceDecayLength", "parRentInfluenceDecayLength_CutOffMultiple",
                    "parNumCitizens", "parNumActivities", "parPeoplePerCitizen", "parVOTMean", "parVOTSpread", "parVOMMean", "parVOMSpread", 
                    "parActivityVOMMean", "parActivityVOMSpread", "parActivityVOLMean", "parActivityVOLSpread"};

// 1. Read and check the whole file before creating anything, so a bad or outdated file leaves the model untouched
List<String[]> savedCitizens = new ArrayList<>();
List<String[]> savedActivities = new ArrayList<>();
List<String[]> savedLinks = new ArrayList<>();
try {
    List<String> lines = java.nio.file.Files.readAllLines(f.toPath());
    Set<String> ignoredSet = new HashSet<>(Arrays.asList(ignored));
    List<String> mismatches = new ArrayList<>();
    for (String line : lines) {
        String[] v = line.split("\t");
        switch (v[0]) {
            case "PARAM":
                if (ignoredSet.contains(v[1])) break;
                Object nowValue = getParameter(v[1]);   // null if the parameter no longer exists. Stored as Object first: passed straight into
                String now = String.valueOf(nowValue);  // String.valueOf, Java would pick its char[] version and fail on numbers
                String saved = v.length > 2 ? v[2] : "";
                if (!saved.equals(now)) mismatches.add(v[1] + " (saved " + saved + ", now " + now + ")");
                break;
            case "CITIZEN":  savedCitizens.add(v); break;
            case "ACTIVITY": savedActivities.add(v); break;
            case "LINK":     savedLinks.add(v); break;
        }
    }
    if (!mismatches.isEmpty()) {
        traceln("Saved state not used, parameters differ: " + String.join(", ", mismatches));
        return false;
    }
    if (savedLinks.size() != links.size()) {
        traceln("Saved state not used: it has " + savedLinks.size() + " links, the current network has " + links.size());
        return false;
    }
    for (String[] v : savedLinks) {
        int ka = Integer.parseInt(v[1]), kb = Integer.parseInt(v[2]);
        if (funFindLink(varGrid[ka / parCols][ka % parCols], varGrid[kb / parCols][kb % parCols]) == null) {
            traceln("Saved state not used: it belongs to a different road network");
            return false;
        }
    }
} catch (Exception e) {
    traceln("Could not read saved state: " + e.getMessage());
    return false;
}

// 2. Activities first (in saved order, so each citizen's weight positions match activity indices)
for (String[] v : savedActivities) {
    int k = Integer.parseInt(v[1]);
    GridPoint g = varGrid[k / parCols][k % parCols];
    Activity a = add_activities();   // preferences set from the file below
    a.parVOM = Double.parseDouble(v[2]);
    a.parVOL = Double.parseDouble(v[3]);
    a.varLocation = g;
    g.colActivities.add(a);
    funPlaceIcon(a, g);
}

// 3. Citizens
for (String[] v : savedCitizens) {
    int k = Integer.parseInt(v[1]);
    GridPoint g = varGrid[k / parCols][k % parCols];
    Citizen c = add_citizens();   // preferences set from the file below
    c.parVOT = Double.parseDouble(v[2]);
    c.parVOM = Double.parseDouble(v[3]);
    c.parVOP = Double.parseDouble(v[4]);
    c.varExpectedWelfare = Double.parseDouble(v[5]);   // needed by the first funCheckWelfarePeak, before the citizen has had a turn
    c.varActivityWeights = new double[v.length - 6];
    for (int a = 0; a < c.varActivityWeights.length; a++) c.varActivityWeights[a] = Double.parseDouble(v[6 + a]);
    c.varHome = g;
    g.colResidents.add(c);
    funPlaceIcon(c, g);
}

// 4. Links: saved impedance (replaces funInitImpedance's draw) and flow, so the first assignment warm-starts
for (String[] v : savedLinks) {
    int ka = Integer.parseInt(v[1]), kb = Integer.parseInt(v[2]);
    Link l = funFindLink(varGrid[ka / parCols][ka % parCols], varGrid[kb / parCols][kb % parCols]);
    l.varImpedance = Double.parseDouble(v[3]);
    l.funUpdateCapacity();
    l.varFlowVol = Double.parseDouble(v[4]);
    l.funUpdateTravelTime();
}

varInitialising = false;         // the city is already settled: no initialisation phase
varStateSaved = true;            // already on file: don't save it again
varAtLoadedEquilibrium = true;   // first checkpoint goes straight to investment
traceln("Saved state loaded: " + activities.size() + " activities, " + citizens.size() + " citizens, " + savedLinks.size() + " links");
return true;
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794412775555</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[testPrintVCRatio]]></Name>
					<X>840</X><Y>1380</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// TEMPORARY TEST. Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). No arguments. Called by funPrintFinalReports.
// Volume / capacity (V/C) over the network, from each link's current equilibrium flow (varFlowVol) and capacity (varCapacity):
// Links with no flow are left out entirely.
//   simple average over used links (each used link counts equally),
//   flow-weighted average (sum of V^2/C over sum of V: the V/C a typical trip experiences, so busy links count more),
//   maximum, and the share of links over capacity (V/C > 1).
double sumVC = 0, sumFlow = 0, sumFlowVC = 0, maxVC = 0;
int count = 0, overCapacity = 0;
for (Link l : links) {
    if (l.varCapacity <= 0) continue;   // safety: capacity not set
    if (l.varFlowVol <= 0) continue;    // empty link: left out
    double vc = l.varFlowVol / l.varCapacity;
    sumVC += vc;
    sumFlow += l.varFlowVol;
    sumFlowVC += l.varFlowVol * vc;
    maxVC = max(maxVC, vc);
    if (vc > 1) overCapacity++;
    count++;
}
if (count == 0) {
    funRuntimePrint("V/C report: no used links");
    return;
}
funRuntimePrint("Turn " + varTurnCount + " V/C over " + count + " used links (of " + links.size() + "): average " + roundToDecimal(sumVC / count, 3)
        + ", flow-weighted average " + roundToDecimal(sumFlow > 0 ? sumFlowVC / sumFlow : 0, 3)
        + ", max " + roundToDecimal(maxVC, 3) + ", links over capacity " + overCapacity
        + " (" + roundToDecimal(100.0 * overCapacity / count, 1) + "%)");   // TEST
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794430388752</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funResumeFromEquilibrium]]></Name>
					<X>850</X><Y>1160</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). No arguments.
// Puts the model into a standard "resume" state at the first spread equilibrium, so a run that loads the saved state and
// a run that went straight through continue identically from here. Called from two places:
//   - Main on startup, on the loaded path (after funLoadState and the land setup), before the first checkpoint.
//   - funRunCheckpoint, in the straight-through run, right after funSaveState at its first equilibrium.
// Both paths then hold the same agents, preferences, links and land; this function makes everything else match:
//   1. Reseed with parSeed + 2: both continue on the same random sequence.
//   2. Rebuild the density surface from scratch: the straight-through run's surface was built up move by move, and its
//      rounding differs slightly from a fresh build, which could flip a later choice.
//   3. Reshuffle the relocation queue (draws from the new seed).
//   4. Reset the turn and round counters, the moves-since-assignment counter and the spread history, so checkpoints,
//      re-assignments and rounds fall on the same turns in both runs.
//   5. Record the first-equilibrium spread (varFirstEquilibriumSpread), the baseline for the final spread report.
//      This function runs exactly once per run, at the first equilibrium on both paths, with identical agents.
//   Traffic reassignment is necessary so that loaded runs and through-runs resume from same flow data (so the through-run doesn't use flow data that may be a few relocations old). That assignment takes place in the checkpoint function that calls the present function. 
// Step 2 draws no random numbers, so the reseed only has to come before the shuffle.
getDefaultRandomGenerator().setSeed(parSeed + 2);
funBuildDensitySurface();
funShuffleResetRelocationQueue();
varTurnCount = 0;
varRounds = 0;
varRelocationsSinceAssignment = 0;
varAssignmentCount = 0;
colAverageSpread.clear();
varFirstEquilibriumSpread = funComputeSpread();
funRuntimePrint("Resumed from equilibrium: reseeded with parSeed + 2, density and queue rebuilt, counters reset");
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794477741774</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funRemoveLink]]></Name>
					<X>120</X><Y>860</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Parameter>
						<Name><![CDATA[l]]></Name>
						<Type><![CDATA[Link]]></Type>
					</Parameter>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Just action (returns nothing). Arguments: l (Link)
// Unregisters link l from both its nodes and deletes it (the reverse of funAddLink)
l.parNodeA.colLinks.remove(l);
l.parNodeB.colLinks.remove(l);
remove_links(l);
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>RETURNS_VALUE</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[boolean]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794499548620</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funCheckWelfarePeak]]></Name>
					<X>970</X><Y>1320</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Returns value, type: boolean. No arguments. Called by funRunCheckpoint at each spread equilibrium.
// Returns true once citizen welfare is in sustained decline, i.e. further investment is making citizens worse off.
//
// Measure: mean over all citizens of varExpectedWelfare (logsum stored on each citizen's last turn, rand per month).
// After an investment, the next check only comes once the spread has settled again, so every citizen has had a turn
// since the investment. On the loaded path the values come from savedState.txt (funLoadState), so the first check
// matches the straight-through run.
//
// Each check's mean is appended to colWelfareHistory (Collection in Main: ArrayList of Double), one value per check:
// the first is the no-investment city, then one after each investment. Unlike the spread history it is never cleared.
// Decline rule: a straight line is fitted (least squares) through the last K = parWelfareSlopeWindow values,
// with x = 0, 1, ..., K-1 (check number) and y = mean welfare:
//   slope = sum((x - x_mean) * (y - y_mean)) / sum((x - x_mean)^2)      (rand per month, per investment)
//   - slope < -parWelfareSlopeThreshold: sustained decline, return true (stop investing).
//   - otherwise: return false (keep investing). Also false until there are K values.
// Every point in the window counts, so one noisy check can't stop the run on its own.
// The best mean so far and the check it came from are kept in varBestMeanWelfare and varBestWelfareCheck
// (checks are numbered from 1: check 1 = no investment, check k = after k-1 investments),
// so the optimum can be reported even though the stop comes later.
// Uses Main variables varBestMeanWelfare (double, initial value Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY) and varBestWelfareCheck (int),
// and Main parameters parWelfareSlopeWindow (int, at least 2, e.g. 5) and parWelfareSlopeThreshold (double, rand per month, e.g. 0).

double sum = 0;
for (Citizen c : citizens) sum += c.varExpectedWelfare;
double meanW = sum / citizens.size();

colWelfareHistory.add(meanW);
int n = colWelfareHistory.size();   // number of checks so far, which is also this check's number (1 = no investment yet)
if (meanW > varBestMeanWelfare) {
    varBestMeanWelfare = meanW;
    varBestWelfareCheck = n;
}

int window = parWelfareSlopeWindow;
if (n < window) {   // not enough history yet to judge a trend
    funRuntimePrint("Mean citizen welfare " + roundToDecimal(meanW, 1) + " at check " + n + " (turn " + varTurnCount + "). Best mean welfare so far: "
            + roundToDecimal(varBestMeanWelfare, 1) + ", at check " + varBestWelfareCheck + "; slope not calculated until " + window + " checks are recorded");
    return false;
}

// Least-squares slope through the last 'window' values (x = 0 .. window-1)
int first = n - window;                    // index of the oldest value in the window
double xMean = (window - 1) / 2.0;         // mean of 0, 1, ..., window-1. From arithmetic sum formula (Gauss method derives this)
double ySum = 0;
for (int i = first; i < n; i++) ySum += colWelfareHistory.get(i);
double yMean = ySum / window;
double sxy = 0, sxx = 0;
for (int i = first; i < n; i++) {
    double dx = (i - first) - xMean;
    sxy += dx * (colWelfareHistory.get(i) - yMean);
    sxx += dx * dx;
}
double slope = sxy / sxx;   // rand per month, per investment
boolean declining = slope < -parWelfareSlopeThreshold; // Slope being less than threshold means more negative, therefore greater decline.

funRuntimePrint("Mean citizen welfare " + roundToDecimal(meanW, 1) + " at check " + n + " (turn " + varTurnCount + "), slope over last "
        + window + " checks " + roundToDecimal(slope, 2) + " per investment (threshold -" + parWelfareSlopeThreshold + ")"
        + (declining ? ": sustained decline" : "") + ", best " + roundToDecimal(varBestMeanWelfare, 1) + " at check " + varBestWelfareCheck);
return declining;
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>RETURNS_VALUE</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794593428083</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funComputeSpread]]></Name>
					<X>720</X><Y>1360</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>false</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Main. Returns value, type: double. No arguments.
// The citizens' spread: the standard distance of their homes from the citizens' mean position (centroid), in metres,
//   spread = sqrt( (1/N) * sum over citizens of ((x - x_mean)^2 + (y - y_mean)^2) )   (the 2D standard deviation of positions)
// A compact city has a small spread; expansion raises it and contraction lowers it.
// Used by funCheckSpreadEquilibrium (equilibrium check) and testPrintSpread (final report), so both measure it the same way.

// Centroid of the citizens' homes (grid steps), then the mean squared distance from it
double sumX = 0, sumY = 0;
for (Citizen c : citizens) {
    sumX += c.varHome.parXIndex;
    sumY += c.varHome.parYIndex;
}
int nCit = citizens.size();
double meanX = sumX / nCit;
double meanY = sumY / nCit;
double sumSq = 0;
for (Citizen c : citizens) {
    double dx = c.varHome.parXIndex - meanX;
    double dy = c.varHome.parYIndex - meanY;
    sumSq += dx * dx + dy * dy;
}
return sqrt(sumSq / nCit) * parStepLength;   // spread in metres
]]></Body>
				</Function>
			</Functions>

