			<Functions>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>RETURNS_VALUE</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1793641074174</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funFreeFlowTime]]></Name>
					<X>160</X><Y>340</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>true</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Link. Returns value, type: double. No arguments.
// Free-flow travel time on this link in minutes: length / speed, where speed = parVRef / impedance.
double v = main.parVRef / varImpedance;   // parVRef already converted to m/min
return parLength / v; //time = distance / speed [minutes]]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1793641102350</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funUpdateCapacity]]></Name>
					<X>160</X><Y>360</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>true</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Link. Just action (returns nothing). No arguments. Call whenever the impedance changes.
// Sets this link's number of lanes and its capacity from its impedance:
//   varLanes    = parImpedanceLocal / I   (a local road has 1 lane; lower impedance = more lanes. Fractions stand for
//                                          wider, faster lanes, so lanes need not be whole numbers)
//   varCapacity = varLanes * (3600 / 2) / (parPeakHourConcentration * parPeoplePerCitizen)
// 3600 / 2: one vehicle per lane every 2 seconds (minimum peak headway) = 1800 vehicles per lane per hour.
// Link flows are counted in citizens (each citizen's activity weights sum to 1, one one-way trip) when they should be multiplied by parPeoplePerCitizen to reflect that each citizen represents a cerain number of real people (too many to simulate one-one). 
// The sub-utilities themselves don't need to be multiplied by parPeoplePerCitizen, since they represent sub-utilities per person evaluating, and if we multiplied them, then each term (rent, time, cost) would change by the same proportion; we would just adjust the logit scale to compensate, and the net result would be identical.
//   parPeakHourConcentration share of the computed trips that fall in the peak hour (0 to 1, default 0.5), which is where we are evaluating in the in the traffic assignments for utility calculations:
//                            higher = traffic more concentrated in the peak = more congestion
// Rather than scaling every flow by parPeoplePerCitizen and parPeakHourConcentration, capacity is divided by both instead (same V/C), so V/C in BPR (funUpdateTravelTime)
// is the real peak-hour V/C.
// Free-flow speed stays parVRef / I (funFreeFlowTime). Road land per node uses varLanes (funNodeRoadLand).
varLanes = main.parImpedanceLocal / varImpedance;
varCapacity = varLanes * (3600.0 / 2) / (main.parPeakHourConcentration * main.parPeoplePerCitizen);
]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>VOID</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1793641113744</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funUpdateTravelTime]]></Name>
					<Description><![CDATA[Bureau of Public Roads (BPR) congestion function]]></Description>
					<X>160</X><Y>380</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>true</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Link. Just action (returns nothing). No arguments.
// Bureau of Public Roads (BPR) congestion function: sets varTravelTime from the free-flow time and the volume/capacity ratio.
//   t = t0 * (1 + parCongestionAlpha * (V / C)^parCongestionBeta)
varTravelTime = funFreeFlowTime() * (1 + main.parCongestionAlpha * pow(varFlowVol / varCapacity, main.parCongestionBeta));]]></Body>
				</Function>
				<Function AccessType="default" StaticFunction="false">
					<ReturnModificator>RETURNS_VALUE</ReturnModificator>
					<ReturnType><![CDATA[double]]></ReturnType>
					<Id>1794650354624</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[funNodeRoadLand]]></Name>
					<X>160</X><Y>400</Y>
					<Label><X>10</X><Y>0</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>false</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>true</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>true</ShowLabel>
					<Body><![CDATA[// Function in Link. Returns value, type: double. No arguments.
// Land this road takes from EACH of its two end nodes (the road's land is split equally between them), in m^2:
//   0.5 * length * width * parCarLandUsage,   width = parRoadWidthRef * varLanes
// parRoadWidthRef: width of road with one lane each way(m). parCarLandUsage: multiplier for the land the road takes beyond its
// carriageway (verges, pavements, parking, junctions...). Road land grows linearly with lanes.
// Uses varLanes, so funUpdateCapacity must have run since the last impedance change (funApplyImpedanceChange,
// funInitImpedance and funLoadState all call it before any land is computed).
return 0.5 * parLength * main.parRoadWidthRef * varLanes * main.parCarLandUsage;
]]></Body>
				</Function>
			</Functions>

